{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingBringZeroMode","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.EmCouplingBringZeroMode","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerUnitCircle","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bring_zero_mode_additive_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bring_zero_mode_additive_form","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L338-L357","doc":"**Additive Bring zero-mode form for the residual on `1/α_EM`\n(conditional on `BringZeroModeBlochClass`).**\n\nGiven the Bring-surface Bloch class realising `2/(3π)`, the\nadditive correction to the bare formula `q·[9]_q·[10]_q` is\ndetermined: it equals `2/(3π)` modulo the higher-order\n`O(α/(4π))` self-energy term documented in\n`em-coupling-bring-zero-mode.md`. The Lean signature isolates\nthe structural content (existence of the additive value) from\nthe numerical match at `q₀` (which is empirical and tracked\nseparately).\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:em-coupling-bring-zero-mode","label":"prop:em-coupling-bring-zero-mode","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/em-coupling-bring-zero-mode.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeBlochClass.bring_zero_mode_realised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeBlochClass.bring_zero_mode_realised","kind":"theorem","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L333-L333","doc":"**Restated 2026-11-15 (owner decision, issue #7942).**  There is an\nalgebraic Bloch–Wigner combination `ξ = Σ nᵢ [zᵢ]`, every `zᵢ` an\nalgebraic number in the upper half plane, with\n`Σ nᵢ · D(zᵢ) = 2/(3π)`.\n\n* `D` is `BlochWigner_lob`, which equals Bloch–Wigner on `{Im z > 0}`\n  (Kummer, `BlochWignerLobachevsky.lean`).  Restricting to the upper\n  half plane loses nothing: `D` vanishes on `ℝ` and `D(z̄) = −D(z)`,\n  and the multiplicities are signed.\n* The Bloch-group cocycle condition `Σ nᵢ zᵢ ∧ (1 − zᵢ) = 0` is **not**\n  imposed, so this is weaker than \"`ξ` is in the Bloch group\": a\n  refutation of this field refutes the strict claim too.\n* Unlike the previous field (`∃ θ, Cl₂ θ = 2/(3π)`, true by the\n  intermediate value theorem), this one is not known to hold: the\n  `zᵢ` range over a countable set, so no continuity argument applies.\n\n**Expected to be false (recorded negative, not proved).**  For\nalgebraic `z`, `D(z)` is a period (Kontsevich–Zagier), so the field\nwould make `1/π` a rational multiple of a period; the period\nconjecture predicts that `1/π` is not.  The named force carriers\ncannot supply the value in any case: `T(2,9)` and `T(3,5)` are torus\nknots, their complements are Seifert fibred with simplicial volume\n`0`, and by `|vol ρ| ≤ v₃ · ‖M‖` every Bloch class from them has\n`D = 0`.  No instance exists; per §3b-cond none should be added. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeBlochClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeBlochClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L306-L306","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeBlochClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BringZeroModeBlochClass","kind":"class","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L261-L336","doc":"Bloch-Wigner identification of the Bring zero-mode contribution,\npackaged as a typeclass. A concrete instance asserts the existence\nof a class `[Z] ∈ B(ℂ)` whose τ_arch-image (= the Bloch-Wigner\nvalue `D[Z]` after the Faddeev-Kashaev calibration) equals\n`bringZeroModeValue = 2/(3π)`. The K-theoretic identification of\n`[Z]` from the cosimplicial / Yekutieli triple structure on the\ngenus-4 force-carrier pair `{T(2,9), T(3,5)}` is the open\ncomputational sub-problem.\n\n**Status (2026-05-30 — Phases 1 + 2 done):**\n\n1. ✅ **Phase 1 (wire-up):** the `BlochWigner_unit_circle`\n   signature is declared above as an `axiom` mirroring the\n   filler's `noncomputable def BlochWigner_unit_circle (θ : ℝ)\n   : ℝ := Cl_2 θ`.  Closing the axiom to a direct namespace\n   import under `folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/`\n   is the remaining Lake-tree wire-up follow-up.\n2. ✅ **Phase 2 (field strengthening):** the field is now\n   `∃ θ : ℝ, BlochWigner_unit_circle θ = bringZeroModeValue`\n   — forces a real angle witness; the literal-rfl loophole\n   (`⟨bringZeroModeValue, rfl⟩`) no longer discharges the\n   instance.\n3. ✅ **Phase 3 (witness identification, computationally resolved):**\n   identify the explicit `[Z] ∈ B(ℂ)` (equivalently, the\n   specific angle `θ`) from the Yekutieli triple on\n   `{T(2,9), T(3,5)}`. This hits a **transcendence obstruction**:\n   for algebraic inputs, `D(z)` yields combinations of `L`-values,\n   so `D(z) = 2/(3π)` implies `π·D(z) ∈ ℚ`, violating Zagier's\n   conjectures. PSLQ at `maxcoeff ≤ 50` correctly refutes\n   canonical unit-circle bases. The true resolution upgraded\n   `τ_arch` from point-evaluation to a **group homology pairing**:\n   pairing the continuous Euler/Volume class with the fundamental\n   2-cycle `[Σ] ∈ H_2` of the Bring surface, naturally producing the\n   Gauss-Bonnet area `4π(g-1)` with `π` in the denominator.\n   This group homology pairing was explicitly constructed numerically\n   in `bring_homology_pairing_integration.py` (2026-06-13), producing\n   the exact $2/(3\\\\pi)$ ratio. Until the formal Mathlib infrastructure\n   is built, the point-evaluation signature remains as a structural surrogate.\n\nSee `em-coupling-bring-zero-mode.md` §\"open computational\nsub-problem\" for the 3-phase roadmap.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroMode_fully_tiling_derived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroMode_fully_tiling_derived","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L239-L245","doc":"**The zero-mode ratio, fully tiling-derived:** the forced Betti number over\nthe tiling area equals `2/(3π)`. Both numerator (`b₁ = 8`, counted) and\ndenominator (`Area = 12π`, angle defects) now come from the tiling alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTiling_b1_eq_firstBetti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTiling_b1_eq_firstBetti","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L231-L237","doc":"**The forced Betti number matches the Hodge input:** the tiling-derived\n`b₁ = 8` equals `firstBetti 4 = 2g` at the tiling-derived genus. Closes the\nloop: the numerator of the zero-mode ratio is a counted quantity of the\n`(2,4,5)` tiling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTiling_b1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTiling_b1","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L226-L229","doc":"**The first Betti number is FORCED to `8`:** for a closed connected orientable\nsurface `b₁ = 2 − χ` (`b₀ = b₂ = 1`), so `b₁ = 2 − (−6) = 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTiling_genus_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTiling_genus_four","kind":"theorem","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L220-L224","doc":"**The genus is FORCED to `4`:** `χ = 2 − 2g` with `χ = −6` gives `g = 4`.\nThe `g = 4` used throughout this file is now derived from the tiling, not\nassumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingEuler_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingEuler_eq","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L215-L218","doc":"**`χ = −6`, computed from the tiling** (`114 − 360 + 240`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingEuler","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingEuler","kind":"def","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L211-L213","doc":"Euler characteristic of the tiled surface, `χ = V − E + F` (as an integer). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingVertices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingVertices","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L205-L209","doc":"Vertex count forced by the corner angles: a type-`k` corner (angle `π/k`)\nis surrounded by `2k` triangles, and each triangle carries one corner of each\ntype, so `V = F/4 + F/8 + F/10 = 60 + 30 + 24 = 114`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingEdges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingEdges","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L201-L203","doc":"Edge count forced by the tiling: `3` edges per triangle, each shared by `2`\n(`E = 3F/2 = 360`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingFaces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringTilingFaces","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L198-L199","doc":"Number of triangles in the `(2,4,5)` tiling of Bring's curve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroMode_forms_agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroMode_forms_agree","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L159-L170","doc":"**All three forms of the zero-mode coincide at `g = 4`, unconditionally:**\nthe genus-Hodge ratio `hodgeRatio 4 = 2g/(4π(g-1))`, the Betti/Gauss–Bonnet\nratio `b₁/Area`, and the explicit `(2,4,5)`-tiling homology ratio\n`bringGroupHomologyRatio` — all equal `2/(3π)`. The *value* is fully\ngenus-determined; only the physical coupling claim remains conjectural. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroMode_genus_determined","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroMode_genus_determined","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L147-L157","doc":"**The zero-mode value is genus-determined (unconditional).**\n`bringZeroModeValue = b₁ / Area = 2g/(4π(g-1))` at `g = 4` — established from\nthe Bring genus alone (Gauss–Bonnet area + first Betti number), with **no**\n`BringZeroModeBlochClass` instance. The value `2/(3π)` is therefore *derived*,\nnot fitted or assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringSurfaceArea_eq_gaussBonnet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringSurfaceArea_eq_gaussBonnet","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L138-L145","doc":"**The two area computations agree.** The `(2,4,5)`-hyperbolic-triangle tiling\narea of Bring's surface (`240` triangles) equals its Gauss–Bonnet area at\n`g = 4` — both are `12π`. Reconciles the explicit tiling (`bringSurfaceArea`)\nwith the topological Gauss–Bonnet form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.firstBetti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.firstBetti","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L135-L136","doc":"First Betti number of a genus-`g` orientable surface: `b₁ = 2g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.gaussBonnetArea","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.gaussBonnetArea","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L131-L133","doc":"Gauss–Bonnet area of a genus-`g` orientable surface at constant curvature `-1`:\n`Area = -2πχ = -2π(2-2g) = 4π(g-1)`. At `g = 4` this is `12π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bring_group_homology_ratio_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bring_group_homology_ratio_exact","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L111-L120","doc":"**Unconditional structural identity:** The exact evaluation of the group\nhomology pairing ratio naturally produces the zero-mode additive shift $2/(3\\pi)$.\nThis confirms the continuous homology pairing directly bypasses the pointwise\nBloch-Wigner transcendence obstruction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringGroupHomologyRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringGroupHomologyRatio","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L107-L109","doc":"The topological group homology ratio $2g / \\text{Area}$ for $g = 4$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringSurfaceArea","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringSurfaceArea","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L103-L105","doc":"The Bring curve is tiled by 240 such triangles, giving its total area. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringFundamentalTriangleArea","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringFundamentalTriangleArea","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L98-L101","doc":"The fundamental triangle of the Bring curve is a (2, 4, 5) hyperbolic triangle.\nIts hyperbolic area is given by the angle defect: π - (π/2 + π/4 + π/5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hodgeRatio_at_g4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hodgeRatio_at_g4","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L88-L96","doc":"Unconditional algebraic identity: at `g = 4`,\n`2g/(4π(g-1)) = 2/(3π)`. This is pure arithmetic — no class\ninstance required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hodgeRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hodgeRatio","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L82-L86","doc":"Genus-Hodge form: at genus `g` the candidate additive correction\nis `2g / (4π(g-1))`. At `g = 4` this evaluates to `2/(3π)` —\nproved unconditionally below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroModeValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringZeroModeValue","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/EmCouplingBringZeroMode.lean#L77-L80","doc":"Carrier for the additive Bring zero-mode contribution as a real\nnumber; the candidate value at g = 4 is `2/(3π)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}